{
  "title": "Number of Provinces",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "type": "matrix",
  "tags": [
    "Graph",
    "DFS",
    "Union-Find"
  ],
  "description": "Given an n x n adjacency matrix isConnected, return the number of provinces (connected components).",
  "target": 2,
  "pseudocode": "1. count = 0\n2. visited = new Set()\n3. for i from 0 to n-1:\n4.   if i not in visited:\n5.     count++\n6.     dfs(i, visited, isConnected)\n7. function dfs(node, visited, isConnected):\n8.   visited.add(node)\n9.   for neighbor from 0 to n-1:\n10.    if isConnected[node][neighbor] == 1 and neighbor not in visited:\n11.      dfs(neighbor, visited, isConnected)",
  "steps": [
